      "css": ".ds-head{font-family:\"Roboto Flex\",Roboto,system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--head,#5a2ee6);color:var(--on-head,#fff);padding:20px 16px 18px 20px;border-radius:0 0 36px 36px}.ds-head h1{margin:0;font-size:36px;font-weight:860;font-stretch:116%;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-glance{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:12px}.ds-stat{min-width:84px;min-height:84px;position:relative;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;padding:8px}.ds-stat>span{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;line-height:1.05;font-weight:820}.ds-stat small,.ds-disk small{font-size:12px;font-weight:650}.ds-batt{color:var(--sun,#ffd23f)}.ds-batt>span{color:var(--on-sun,#3a2700);font-size:22px;font-stretch:84%}.ds-link{color:var(--pink,#ffc4ea)}.ds-link>span{color:var(--on-pink,#5c0a45);font-size:12px;font-weight:750}.ds-disk{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;background:var(--mint,#9ff0d3);color:var(--on-mint,#00382a);border-radius:42px;padding:8px 22px;line-height:1.05}.ds-disk b{font-size:24px;font-weight:820;font-stretch:92%}.ds-disk>i{display:block;height:8px;margin-top:7px;border-radius:4px;background:rgb(0 56 42/.18);overflow:hidden}.ds-disk>i>i{display:block;width:78%;height:100%;background:var(--on-mint,#00382a);border-radius:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Message Bubbles",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "bubble-mine",
      "description": "His violet message with the bottom-right tail, the Mac's surface reply with the top-left tail.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-thread\"><div class=\"ds-mine\">Clean up my Downloads.</div><div class=\"ds-reply\">Moved 6 installers to the Trash, 3.2 GB in all.</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-thread{font-family:\"Roboto Flex\",Roboto,system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;background:var(--bg,#f5f1ff);padding:14px;font-size:16px;font-weight:450;line-height:1.45}.ds-mine{align-self:flex-end;max-width:86%;background:var(--primary,#5a2ee6);color:var(--on-primary,#fff);padding:12px 18px;border-radius:28px 28px 8px 28px;transition:border-radius .4s,transform .4s}.ds-mine:active{transform:scale(.98);border-radius:20px 20px 8px 20px}.ds-reply{align-self:flex-start;max-width:92%;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--ink,#1a1530);padding:14px 18px;border-radius:8px 28px 28px 28px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Offline Banner",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "banner-offline",
      "description": "Red container with a clover mark, the reason, and Open Tailscale and Try Again.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-banner\"><span class=\"ds-mark\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M50.00 2.00L53.12 2.34L56.14 3.34L58.97 4.93L61.52 7.00L63.77 9.44L65.70 12.10L67.35 14.82L68.77 17.49L70.05 19.99L71.30 22.24L72.61 24.22L74.08 25.92L75.78 27.39L77.76 28.70L80.01 29.95L82.51 31.23L85.18 32.65L87.90 34.30L90.56 36.23L93.00 38.48L95.07 41.03L96.66 43.86L97.66 46.88L98.00 50.00L97.66 53.12L96.66 56.14L95.07 58.97L93.00 61.52L90.56 63.77L87.90 65.70L85.18 67.35L82.51 68.77L80.01 70.05L77.76 71.30L75.78 72.61L74.08 74.08L72.61 75.78L71.30 77.76L70.05 80.01L68.77 82.51L67.35 85.18L65.70 87.90L63.77 90.56L61.52 93.00L58.97 95.07L56.14 96.66L53.12 97.66L50.00 98.00L46.88 97.66L43.86 96.66L41.03 95.07L38.48 93.00L36.23 90.56L34.30 87.90L32.65 85.18L31.23 82.51L29.95 80.01L28.70 77.76L27.39 75.78L25.92 74.08L24.22 72.61L22.24 71.30L19.99 70.05L17.49 68.77L14.82 67.35L12.10 65.70L9.44 63.77L7.00 61.52L4.93 58.97L3.34 56.14L2.34 53.12L2.00 50.00L2.34 46.88L3.34 43.86L4.93 41.03L7.00 38.48L9.44 36.23L12.10 34.30L14.82 32.65L17.49 31.23L19.99 29.95L22.24 28.70L24.22 27.39L25.92 25.92L27.39 24.22L28.70 22.24L29.95 19.99L31.23 17.49L32.65 14.82L34.30 12.10L36.23 9.44L38.48 7.00L41.03 4.93L43.86 3.34L46.88 2.34Z\"/></svg><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" style=\"position:relative\"><path d=\"M3 9.5a13 13 0 0 1 18 0M6 13a8.5 8.5 0 0 1 12 0M9 16.5a4 4 0 0 1 6 0\"/></svg></span><p>Can't reach the Mac.</p><button class=\"ds-btn ds-filled\">Open Tailscale</button><button class=\"ds-btn ds-tonal\">Try Again</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-banner{font-family:\"Roboto Flex\",Roboto,system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 14px;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:28px;background:var(--fail-c,#ffdad6);color:var(--on-fail-c,#5c0a07)}.ds-mark{position:relative;width:44px;height:44px;display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--fail,#c62828)}.ds-mark>svg:last-child{color:var(--on-fail,#fff);width:22px;height:22px}.ds-banner p{margin:0;flex:1 1 180px;font-size:16px}.ds-btn{font-family:\"Roboto Flex\",Roboto,system-ui,sans-serif;min-height:48px;padding:0 20px;border:0;border-radius:24px;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer;transition:border-radius .35s}.ds-btn:active{border-radius:12px}.ds-btn:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#5a2ee6);outline-offset:2px}.ds-filled{background:var(--fail,#c62828);color:var(--on-fail,#fff)}.ds-tonal{background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--ink,#1a1530)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Loudest Native App on the Phone",
    "overview": "The page is Pixel's own Material 3 Expressive with the volume turned all the way up. It should feel like it shipped with the Fold, and still carry more colour and more shape than anything else on the phone. A tall violet header owns the top, pastel containers carry the Mac's numbers and the shortcuts, and every state the agent can be in has its own shape and colour, so he can read the screen from arm's length without reading a word.\n\nIt's a working tool he uses all day, one-handed on the outer screen. Density is moderate: big type and big targets, but no decorative space. Colour always means something. Violet is him and the app, green is work going on, amber is waiting on him, red is broken or stopping, and the four pastels are the Mac's figures and his shortcuts. The grey chat with one blue accent is the thing this refuses.\n\nMotion is springy and short, and it's tied to state. Shapes morph when the state behind them changes, corners tighten under a finger, and nothing loops unless the Mac is actually busy or waiting on him.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Violet header block with The Lab in heavy, wide Roboto Flex and three stat shapes",
      "Tonal cards with 28 px corners, no borders, depth from tone rather than shadow",
      "One morphing shape library where each shape names a state",
      "Fat pill composer with colour-cycled shortcut chips riding on top",
      "Spring timing on shape and corner changes, still shapes under reduced motion",
      "Light and dark from one set of `light-dark()` tokens"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Paired Ink Rule",
        "body": "Every fill has its own ink token (`mint` with `on-mint`, `head` with `on-head`). Changing a fill means checking its ink at 4.5:1 for text, and changing both if it falls short. \"Make the header green\" is a change to `head`, `head-deep` and maybe `on-head`, nothing else.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Colour Rule",
        "body": "Green, amber and red say what the agent is doing. Don't use them for decoration, and don't use the pastels or violet for a state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Token Rule",
        "body": "Colours are written once as `light-dark(light, dark)` in `:root`. Never hard-code a colour in a rule, and never add a `prefers-color-scheme` block. `html[data-theme]` forces one theme for testing.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Role Token Rule",
        "body": "Sizes and weights come from `--fs-*` and `--fw-*`. Reach for a role, not a number, and keep weights on the six steps (450, 550, 650, 750, 820, 860).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Every changing number (battery, disk, times, durations) sets `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` so it doesn't jiggle as it counts.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Always There Rule",
        "body": "The message box, Stop while working, Allow and Deny on every request, the offline banner and messages still waiting to send must stay on screen and usable in every one of these layouts, with the keyboard up, at large text, folded, unfolded, book and tabletop.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hinge Rule",
        "body": "Nothing he reads or taps crosses `--lab-hinge-*`. A new fixed or absolute element has to have a book and a tabletop answer.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Floaters Rule",
        "body": "A shadow means it floats over scrolling content. Cards in the conversation never get one.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shape Means State Rule",
        "body": "Don't give a state's shape to something that isn't that state. A new state picks an unused shape or reuses its nearest meaning.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Morph Not Swap Rule",
        "body": "Where a shape stays on screen through a state change, as the header stats, the toolbar's loader and the send button do, change its class (`s-cookie` to `s-clover`) on the same path so it morphs instead of replacing the element. Run cards, the request list and answered rows are redrawn when they change, so their new shape just appears.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every control at least 48 px in both directions. Things drawn at 40 px get a `::before` that extends the hit area to 48.",
      "**Do** keep text at 4.5:1 on its fill in both themes. The shipped pairs run from 5.1:1 (`faint` on `bg`, light) to 14.8:1.",
      "**Do** call `lab.ready()` in the first animation frame after the first draw, as `app.js` does now. Never wait for the network, the history or fonts first. Past 8 seconds the phone shows its safe screen.",
      "**Do** pad anything pinned to the bottom with `--lab-inset-bottom` and let it move with the keyboard, without a transition of its own.",
      "**Do** give anything new a folded, unfolded, keyboard, book and tabletop answer before calling it done, and check both themes with `?theme=light` and `?theme=dark`.",
      "**Do** keep the Review and Stop pair, Allow and Deny, and the send button in the bottom half of the folded screen, where the thumb is.",
      "**Do** add icons as stroked 24 px symbols in the sprite in `index.html`.",
      "**Do** keep fonts, images and icons inside `app/`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put the message box, Stop, or Allow and Deny anywhere they can scroll away, hide behind the keyboard or sit under the toolbar.",
      "**Don't** add an animation that runs while nothing is happening. The only loops are the working loaders and the slow waiting burst.",
      "**Don't** animate layout (height, padding, grid) on the header or composer. Snap the layout and animate shape, colour or opacity.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to cards, borders to containers, or square corners.",
      "**Don't** use green, amber or red outside the state they mean, or use a state's shape for something else.",
      "**Don't** reach for a grey chat with one blue accent. Restyle within the colour, shape and type roles above.",
      "**Don't** load anything from the internet. A CDN script or a Google Fonts link won't load on the phone."
    ]
  }
}
